<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63118" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λί̆θ-αξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰκος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stony</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθακι ποτὶ πέτρῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.415
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as fem.
				Subst., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				1112
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				613
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωφὴ λ.</span>, of a
				<i>gravestone,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				7.392
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Heraclid.
			</span></i> Sinop.); of a <i>precious stone</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				6.343
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. τρητὴν σπόγγῳ
			ἐειδομένην</span>, of the pumice-<i>stone,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				6.66
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			in pl., <i>stony land</i>, Epic.in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Arch.Pap.</u>
				7.10
			</span></i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				150
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕρμαξ</span>.</div>
